From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opi5 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rknpu: power off after probe from the delayed work

The power-off at the end of probe waits for the IOMMU to suspend, but
the driver core keeps it resumed until probe returns. The wait timed out
and leaked a runtime PM reference, so the NPU never powered off. Power
off from the delayed work instead.
---
 drivers/rknpu/src/rknpu_drv.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rknpu/src/rknpu_drv.c b/drivers/rknpu/src/rknpu_drv.c
index f6129778bc8f..bb3355fedc35 100644
--- a/drivers/rknpu/src/rknpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/rknpu/src/rknpu_drv.c
@@ -1700,8 +1700,12 @@ static int rknpu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (rknpu_dev->iommu_en)
 		rknpu_iommu_init_domain(rknpu_dev);
 
-	rknpu_power_off(rknpu_dev);
-	atomic_set(&rknpu_dev->power_refcount, 0);
+	/*
+	 * opi5: power off from the delayed work: the driver core keeps the IOMMU
+	 * resumed until probe returns.
+	 */
+	atomic_set(&rknpu_dev->power_refcount, 1);
+	rknpu_power_put_delay(rknpu_dev);
 	atomic_set(&rknpu_dev->cmdline_power_refcount, 0);
 	atomic_set(&rknpu_dev->iommu_domain_refcount, 0);
 
